% verified: Crossref (DOI 10.1016/j.ymssp.2015.04.021) and the published PDF (supplied by the author, 2026-10-09).
% Kept although older than five years: it is the reference analysis of the CWRU data used here and the only
% source for the facts taken from it.
% Statements used in main.tex were checked against: abstract and Sec. 1 (three methods, every record categorised);
% Sec. 2 (slip shifts fault frequencies by up to 1-2%); Sec. 4 (load mainly lowers speed, by almost 4%, no radial
% load); Sec. 6.1.1 (EMI at harmonics of about 4.2 kHz from the dynamometer controller); Sec. 6.2 (outcome depends
% more on assembly than on fault size or speed/load); Table 2 (6205 BSF 2.357; 6203 BPFI 4.947, BPFO 3.053,
% BSF 1.994); Table 3 (records 236DE, 237DE clipped); Table A1 (normal baseline at 48 kHz; 98: 1772 rpm,
% 99: 1750 rpm); Table B2 (DE diagnosis categories of records 118-120, 185-188, 224-225, 198-200 are P or N
% under all three methods; all other fault records used here reach Y1/Y2 with at least one method).
